<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis I, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1708–1765</span> · Also known as Francis Stephen of Lorraine, Francis III Stephen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francis I (1708–1765), born Francis Stephen, was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> from 1729 until 1737, when he gave up the duchy under the settlement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-polish-succession">War of the Polish Succession</a> and received the Grand Duchy of Tuscany in exchange. His marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> in 1736 founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-habsburg-lorraine">House of Habsburg-Lorraine</a>. He was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> in 1745, though his wife held real power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francis-i-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Francis I, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin van Meytens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martin_van_Meytens_006.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
